1 NAME Gunnar Olof /Hyltén-Cavallius/
2 GIVN Gunnar Olof
2 _MARNM Hyltén-Cavallius
1 NAME /Hyltén-Cavallius/
2 GIVN
2 SURN Hyltén-Cavallius
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 18 MAY 1818
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vislanda
3 STAE Kronoberg County
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE 5 JUL 1889
2 ADDR
3 CITY Skatelöv
3 STAE Kronoberg County
3 CTRY Sweden
1 OCCU Etnolog, chargé d'affaires och generalkonsul i Rio de Janeiro, teaterdirektør, Generalkonsul
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Etnolog, (M. Phil. 1839)  chargé d'affaires och svensk/norsk generalkonsul i Rio de Janeiro. Förste direktør vid kungliga teatrarna, godsägare och författare.
2 CONT
2 CONT Head of Victorian gentlemen with full beard, in 3/4 view
2 CONT
2 CONT Born May 18, 1818 Hönetorp, Wislanda socken, Småland, Sweden 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died July 5, 1889 (aged 71) Sunnanvik, Småland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alma mater Uppsala University, MPhil 1839 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notable work(s) Wärend och Wirdarne; ett försök i svensk ethnologi (in Swedish). Stockholm: P.A. Norstedt. 1863-64. Retrieved 2014-03-01.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT Carl Fredrik Cavallius  Anna Elisabet Hyltenius
2 CONT
2 CONT Relatives Bp. Olof Cavallius (1648-1703) (great-grandfather's brother)  Notes  [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunnar Olof Hyltén-Cavallius (1818-1889) was a Swedish scholar of cultural history, librarian, theatre director, and diplomat.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunnar was the son of a clergyman from Vislanda. While he was a student at the Uppsala University,[1] he was impressed with the late currents of Gothicismus.[citation needed] He was an employee at the Swedish Royal Library in the 
2 CONC period 1839-1856, the director of the Royal Theatres, 1856-1860, and the Chargé d'affaires in Empire of Brazil, 1860-1864.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Gunnar was early interested in the collection of fairy tales and legends, and together with George Stephens, he published the first collection of Svenska folksagor och äfventyr in 1844-1849. His main work was Wärend och Wirdarne (
2 CONC 1-2, 1863-1868), which was inspired both by Jacob Grimm's Deutsche Mythologie (1835) and evolutionist theories of Sven Nilsson. Wärend och Wirdarne can be seen as the foundation of Swedish ethnology.
2 CONT
2 CONT During his last years, he lived in the parish of Skatelöv in Småland, and his collections were the foundation of the Museum of Småland in Växjö.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/mobil/Artikel/13941
