1 NOTE {geni:about_me} His widowed mom wed a widower, whose's sister-in-law was my 5th great grandma Karin O.
2 CONT Shown with wife Liz Andersson Fattenborg and their kids at Rickleå 13, AI:2.48 (1746-62). Johnan Klingstrom-Andersson, until early death on Christmas eve 1750, was Gästgivare (innkeeper) in Rickleå, as his father Anders Olsson bef
2 CONC ore him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lövånger Marriage Book: November 15 1738: married Innkeeper (Gästgivaren) from Rickleå Johan Andersson Klingström with the maid (pigan) Elisabet Andersdotter Fattenborg at Kräkånger. Death Registry: Andersson-Klingström, Johan, Ri
2 CONC ckleå, 1749-12-24, 36 years, 30 weeks, Innkeeper (Gästgivare) in the town of Rickleå, Bygdeå parish, Västerbotten.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other deaths in the family:
2 CONT > his son: Klingström, Johan .Rickleå . 1745-12-15. Gästgivare hans son Olof (28 weeks).
2 CONT > his surviving daughter: Klingström, Johan .Rickleå . 1760-12-12
2 CONT ...Avlidne Gästgivaren hans dotter Cajsa Lena (14 år. Andtäppa och Bröstvärk [asthma and catarrh])
2 CONT > his widow: Klingström, Johan .Rickleå . 1789-01-26
2 CONT ..hans ånka (widow) Lisa Fattenborg 70 år Andtäppa & Magflen (asthma and stomach pain)
2 CONT > his surviving brother: Klingström, Nils .Rickleå . 1783-08-31
2 CONT ...Gästgivare (71 år. Andtäppa och Bröstfeber (asthma and pneumonia))
2 CONT > his surviving sister-in-law: Klingström, Nils .Rickleå . 1789-06-26
2 CONT ..Gästgivare hans ånka (widow) Catharina Umin 77 år Rötfeber (gangrene)
2 CONT > his niece: Klingström, Nils .Skinnarbyn daughter Brita 1745-07-22 (40 weeks, 1 day)
2 CONT > himself: Klingström-Andersson, Johan .Rickleå . 1749-12-24  ...Gästgivare (36 år, 30 v)
2 CONT
2 CONT Dombok (Court Judgment Book) Dmb 1748 spring: Nils Andersson Klingström in Skinnarbyn against his brother Johan Andersson Klingström in Rikleå agreed case, regarding that, the innkeeper after avl. mother wife Karin Nilsdotter was 
2 CONC not allowed to draw up a legal inventory...
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Agneta Olofsson, "Bygdeå Byar och Gårdar," p. 336-337, Rikleå 13 continued, cites DII:1.48v and 1748 Dombok.
