0 @I6000000031474858936@ INDI
1 NAME Nathalie /Kavaleff/
2 GIVN Nathalie
2 SURN Kavaleff
2 _MARNM Mankell
2 NICK Natalia
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 29 DEC 1864
2 PLAC Domarby gård
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 Tuomarinkylä
3 CITY Helsinki
3 CTRY Finland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 JAN 1956
2 ADDR
3 CITY Fort Lauderdale
3 STAE Florida
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Phys. MD
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nathalie left Finland on Saturday the 27th Sept. 1890 by S/S Helsingfors as Miss Kavaleff but she arrived to US as Mrs Mankell. I do not know where she married Mankell. The Mankells settled down in Buffalo, NY and 
2 CONC their address was: 63 Linwood Avenue. Carl Gustaf was friend with George Merrit Clark, a painter from Buffalo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathalie graduated from the Royal Gymnastic Central Institute/GCI in Stockholm in 1889 as teacher of gymnastics. After that she was working at Mariehamns Badanstalt, Åland in the Summer 1890. She had also a practice in Helsingfors
2 CONC  at Högbergsgatan 21 before she left Finland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the States she had a practice already 1890 in Buffalo, worked at Franklin School 1894-1903 as teacher of gymnastics, giving lectures in medical gymnastics at the medical department of the University ibm since 1896 and Universit
2 CONC y of Buffalo since 1899. Nathalie graduated from Univ. of Buffalo on 1911 as a doctor with the speciality in medical gymnastics. "Women and athletics gained a foothold through Dr Mankell and by the fall of 1922, enough support was
2 CONC  gathered to establish the University's Women's Athletics Association" (copied from the website of UB). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathalie was naturalized July 25, 1911 at the Southern District Court of New York. C-G (Claude) Mankell 1894 at Erik County.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. Nathalie K. Mankell
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials services for Dr. Nathalie K. Mankell, 91, a former Buffalo and East Aurora resident and pioneer in physical education for women, were held yesterday in First Presbyterian Church, Ft. Lauderdale, Fla. The body is enroute 
2 CONC to East Aurora for burial in Oakwood Cemetery. Dr. Mankell died Monday in Ft. Lauderdale Hospital.
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Finland, Dr. Mankell lectured on physical education in the University of Buffalo and other schools here. Although a 1911 graduate of the University of Buffalo School of Medicine, she did not practice medicine.
2 CONT Her husband, Gustav C Mankell was a commercial artist for the Larkin Co., Inc. After his death in East Aurora in 1936, she moved to Ft. Lauderdale. her only surviving sister living in Finland.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Buffalo, NY. Courier Express, January 11, 1956)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT Mrs. Mankell was a graduate of the Royal Gymnastic Institute of Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/149749505/nathalie-mankell
2 CONT # The Miami Herald, January 10, 1956, Page  15. via Newspapers.com (https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-miami-herald-mankell/148534500/ : accessed June 1, 2024), clip page for Mankell.  “A sister in Finland is the lone survivor
2 CONC .”
