1 NAME Helena Catarina /Israelsdotter/
2 GIVN Helena Catarina
2 SURN Israelsdotter
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 FEB 1825
2 PLAC Ström, Umeå LFS/AC
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 NOV 1894
2 PLAC Nordmaling/AC
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sponsors:
2 CONT Farmer Anders Jonson and his wife and son Emanuel and daughter
2 CONT Helen Dorothea in Ström.
2 CONT
2 CONT Helena is found in the house interrogation registers from 1845, as a maid in Järnäs and then in 1850 as a maid in Levar (indistinct). Her sister Anna married a crofter from Håknäs. In the birth and baptismal register it says that 
2 CONC Eric was born in Håknäs. It may be that some time before Eric's birth, Helena moved to her sister in Håknäs and thus came to settle there. Helena with her son Eric can be found in the house interrogation records from Håknäs 1st ti
2 CONC me in 1858.
2 CONT ---------- Note /Claes Bystedt ------------------
2 CONT We do not know if Helena has been a maid in Levar. Not available in Levar hf at that time. Moved in 1847 to Umeå lfs, and worked as a maid in Västerhiske, Koddis, Ansmark, Sörmjöle and Hörne, before she moved back to Håknäs in 185
2 CONC 5, almost a year before her son was born. See resident notes. If she had been a maid in Levar, she would have had to travel at least 8 km one way every day.
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------
2 CONT According to what our father (Magnus Strömgren) and his sisters told us, Helena had visited Stugunäs sometime in the 1890s. It may have been sometime after Kristina's death in 1893. A memory the children had of their grandmother w
2 CONC as, among other things, when she procured juniper berries and brewed juniper drink. It tasted divine according to what they told me.
2 CONT Helena was apparently good at cooking. It has been said that after participating in larger dinners, she could bring some of the table's delicacies with her on her return home. For this, she had a special food box, which is hand-pa
2 CONC inted and labeled with her name. This casket is now with Gunnel and Yngve in Skravelsjö.
2 CONT /Holger Strömgren
